# DianaSh golden corpus. Recorded from the C# shell, byte for byte; EMUSEN_DIANASH_GOLDEN=record rewrites it - see EmuSen_DianaSh.md §13.4.
# Patterns: <ROOT> is the sandbox's real root, <TEMP> the corpus's real temporary folder, <INSTALL> the install's real directory;
# a 'match' block is a regular expression the whole output must match, written where a line prints a time or a measured number.
command cov
usage 1   cov on|off                    start/stop recording executed addresses
usage 2   cov clear                     forget everything recorded so far
usage 3   cov <addr> [<len>]            report which of <len> bytes from <addr> ever executed
usage 4                                 (default 16); 0 executed means the code never ran
usage 5   cov mark                      remember what has run so far, so `cov new` can subtract it
usage 6   cov new <addr> [<len>]        only what has run SINCE the mark - do the thing, then ask
usage 7   cov funcs [<count>]           routines discovered by watching calls land, busiest first
usage 8   cov save|load <file>          persist the map to Logs/<CoreName>/<file> and merge it back
usage 9   cov <cpu> on|off|clear|<addr> same, on another processor's own instruction stream -
usage 10                                 `cpus` lists them, and each has its own address space

case on the fake target
target fake
covers 1-10
file Logs/GOLDEN/bad.cov 9
not a map
$ cov
out 71
Usage: cov [<cpu>] on|off|clear|mark|new|funcs|save|load|<addr> [<len>]
status 0
action none
$ cov on
out 22
Coverage recording on.
status 0
action none
$ cov 8000
out 62
Coverage $008000-$00800F: 0/16 bytes executed
  Never reached.
status 0
action none
$ cov 8000 4
out 61
Coverage $008000-$008003: 0/4 bytes executed
  Never reached.
status 0
action none
$ cov 8000 0
out 24
Length must be positive.
status 0
action none
$ cov mark
out 90
Coverage marked at 0 instructions - `cov new <addr>` now reports only what runs from here.
status 0
action none
$ cov new 8000
out 95
Coverage $008000-$00800F: 0/16 bytes executed since the mark
  Nothing new here since the mark.
status 0
action none
$ cov new
out 29
Usage: cov new <addr> [<len>]
status 0
action none
$ cov funcs
out 77
No routines discovered yet - nothing has been called since recording started.
status 0
action none
$ cov funcs 4
out 77
No routines discovered yet - nothing has been called since recording started.
status 0
action none
$ cov off
out 48
Coverage recording off, 0 instructions recorded.
status 0
action none
$ cov funcs
out 59
No routines discovered (recording is OFF - `cov on` first).
status 0
action none
$ cov save
out 22
Usage: cov save <file>
status 0
action none
$ cov save map.cov
out 64
Coverage map saved to <ROOT>/Logs/GOLDEN/map.cov (0 routine(s)).
status 0
action none
$ ls Logs/GOLDEN
out 15
bad.cov
map.cov
status 0
action none
$ cov load map.cov
out 77
Coverage map merged from <ROOT>/Logs/GOLDEN/map.cov (0 routine(s) known now).
status 0
action none
$ cov load nosuch.cov
out 49
No coverage map at <ROOT>/Logs/GOLDEN/nosuch.cov.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
$ cov load bad.cov
out 69
<ROOT>/Logs/GOLDEN/bad.cov is not a coverage map this build can read.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
$ cov clear
out 17
Coverage cleared.
status 0
action none
$ cov gsu on
out 26
GSU coverage recording on.
status 0
action none
$ cov gsu 20
out 66
GSU coverage $000020-$00002F: 0/16 bytes executed
  Never reached.
status 0
action none
$ cov cop off
out 52
GSU coverage recording off, 0 instructions recorded.
status 0
action none
$ cov cpu clear
out 17
Coverage cleared.
status 0
action none
$ cov gsu
out 44
Usage: cov <cpu> on|off|clear|<addr> [<len>]
status 0
action none
$ cov zz
out 46
Error: Could not find any recognizable digits.
status 1
action none
end

case new before a mark
target fake
covers 6
$ cov new 8000
out 66
Nothing marked yet - run `cov mark`, do the thing, then ask again.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end

case a bare target
target bare
covers 1,9
$ cov on
out 44
GOLDEN target records no execution coverage.
status 0
action none
$ cov gsu on
out 44
GOLDEN target records no execution coverage.
status 0
action none
$ cov cop on
out 57
This cartridge has no coprocessor to record coverage for.
status 0
action none
end

case with no target
target none
covers 1
$ cov on
out 65
Error: No ROM loaded - this command needs an active debug target.
status 1
action none
$ echo $?
out 1
1
status 0
action none
end

